  </category>
  <category>
    <pattern>GIVE THE STATEMENT AND ONE CONCRETE EXAMPLE STATE WHAT IEC 62304 GOVERNS AND OUTLINE A COMPLIANT SOFTWARE LIFECYCLE FOR A SAMD PRODUCT</pattern>
    <template>IEC 62304 is the international standard for the software lifecycle of medical device software. A compliant lifecycle includes: software safety classification; requirements and architecture; detailed design and implementation; verification (unit/integration/system); risk management linkage (hazards ↔ requirements ↔ tests); configuration management; problem resolution; and maintenance/post-market updates with controlled change impact analysis. Example: external validation across hospitals often reveals performance drops due to protocol differences; recalibration or domain adaptation may be required.</template>
  </category>
